from pathlib import Path
import json,re
root=Path(__file__).parent
rows=json.loads((root/'manifest.json').read_text())
photo_reference="REFERENCE PRESENT: The supplied person/persons are authoritative for identity. Preserve each recognizable face, facial structure, distinguishing features, age, ethnicity, skin tone, natural body proportions and hairline. The PicMagic preview supplies the creative treatment, pose, wardrobe, expression, composition, lighting and environment only; do not copy its model's face or identity. Cultural styling never determines ethnicity. Adapt hair arrangement, clothing, expression and pose only as required by the concept, keeping the person recognizable. Otherwise preserve or gently arrange the existing hair."
art_reference="REFERENCE PRESENT: The supplied person is authoritative for identity. Preserve recognizable facial geometry, eye spacing, distinguishing features, age cues, ethnicity, natural proportions and hairline. Translate their relative complexion values into the explicitly declared paper or ink palette; artistic pigment is not literal photographic skin colour or a change of ethnicity. Keep facial landmarks and marks legible in the new medium. The PicMagic example supplies the art treatment and composition only; never substitute its model's face."
product_reference="PRODUCT REFERENCE: Product fidelity takes priority. Preserve the supplied product's exact geometry, material, colour, design, pattern, weave, stitching, silhouette, label, logo and accessories actually supplied. Use only views supported by the references. Do not invent unseen construction, hide important details or redesign the item to resemble the PicMagic example. Keep model identity separate from product identity. If generated lettering or fine construction changes, use the original product layer in a composite rather than claim exact reproduction."
fallback={'P01':'one adult traveller','P02':'one adult shown in four intentional depictions','P03':'one adult traveller','P04':'three family members with a believable mix of ages','P05':'one adult','P06':'two adults','P08':'one adult designer','P12':'one adult model shown in three intentional depictions','P13':'one adult'}
bodies={
'P01':"Create a travel-memory artwork: the traveller rests an open blank journal on a ghat step. A single curved indigo ink shoreline flows out of the page and becomes the real river behind them. Keep the face, hand and nearest stone photographic; ink never crosses the face or makes the person dissolve. Copper sunset light, cream paper and practical indigo cotton clothing. Frame the journal transition prominently enough to read at small size, with a clear three-quarter portrait and unblocked face. Incidental distant people, if present, are not substitute identity subjects. Do not reproduce private handwriting or add lettering.",
'P02':"Create One Day, Four Possible Worlds as a 3:4 asymmetric composition. Use ONE reference identity in FOUR intentional depictions, not four different people. A dominant portrait in an ochre work shirt fills the left two-thirds. Three unequal curved windows at right show that same person as a night-sky observer beside a telescope, a focused pottery maker shaping one bowl, and a mountain traveller on a winding road. Faces stay readable in every window, with the same age, hairline, face geometry and physique. Clothing and expression may vary naturally; preserve the supplied complexion under neutral face light. No blended bodies or fifth depiction. These are imagined pursuits, not claims of real qualifications. If the reference contains several people, ask which one is intended. Create a stable reference-conditioned scene first; compare identity before assembling the full composition. Keep every panel inside the crop.",
'P03':"Create a controlled double-exposure portrait. Keep the single almost-frontal face fully photographic and naturally illuminated from eyes to mouth. Inside the jacket and outer shoulder silhouette, build slate Himalayan mountain layers, a warm winding road and one tiny unoccupied roadside tent. A pale sky separates facial edges from scenery. The road never crosses eyes or mouth; the face must not appear hollow or dissolving. Exactly one depiction of the reference person, no extra human silhouettes. This is a visual travel metaphor, not evidence of an actual expedition.",
'P04':"Create a shallow handcrafted courtyard model displayed on a substantial wooden shelf. Gather all intended family members around a small chessboard near the front, with each face large enough to read. Preserve the supplied group's actual count, identities and relative ages; the preview's three people do not override a different supplied family. If references are incomplete or conflicting, ask who belongs in the scene. Uniformly reduce the group to miniature scale without changing relative anatomy. Teal balconies, warm plaster, terracotta tiles, visible cutaway walls, carved wood and paper edges establish a handmade memory. Faces remain individually rendered, not blank doll faces. Keep the complete shelf and model in frame. Distant buildings must contain no added family members or portrait faces.",
'P05':"Create a close portrait as a declared two-ink print: plum and saffron on off-white paper stock. One diagonal carriage-window shadow crosses the shoulder, never the eyes. Show coarse halftone and paper fibres, with a slight background registration offset while eye contours and age cues remain crisp. Adapt a plain period collar and a thoughtful outward glance; do not copy an actor or film poster. Decorative marks in the sample are optional styling, not required identity features. Keep actual reference marks recognizable in the print. No titles, invented lettering or photographic-skin instructions that conflict with the ink medium.",
'P06':"Photograph the same two adults exchanging one folded cream letter beside a stationary 1970s-inspired heritage railway carriage. Period is wardrobe and setting only; preserve actual reference ages and identities. Muted maroon and cream travel clothes, worn travel bags, amber platform lamps and cool steam at the far end of the platform. Show separate natural hands supporting opposite ends of the letter, their faces clear and eyes meeting with a quiet relieved smile. Keep steam away from faces and hands. No readable text, copied film composition or actor likeness. If supplied references do not identify the intended two people, ask for clarification rather than inventing a partner.",
'P08':"Create a surreal-scale artwork of the reference person as a miniature designer among enormous mountain-like folds of indigo woven cloth. One oversized pale wooden spool anchors scale; a stitched seam winds like a trail toward a fabric pass. The person stands close in the foreground, large enough for a readable face, with practical rust workwear and a small sewing bag. Scale the whole body uniformly without changing physique or relative anatomy. Coherent contact shadows, visible cloth fibres and woodgrain, soft side light and distant depth falloff. No extra people or tiny anonymous protagonist. This personal artwork does not claim an exact manufactured garment design.",
'P12':"Create One Saree, Three Campaign Worlds: ONE model identity intentionally shown THREE times, wearing the SAME supplied saree and blouse. Establish a stable model-and-garment fixture first and compare it before creating the panels. One dominant front-three-quarter full-length view fills the left two-thirds in a basalt courtyard. Two supporting front-three-quarter views at right show a rain-lit glass pavilion and an ivory sculptural studio. Maintain nearly the same pose and drape so garment differences can be spotted. Neutral light on the garment preserves its actual colour and weave; atmosphere changes the surrounding set. Preserve every supplied border, motif, blouse, stitch and accessory. Do not invent a back view or unseen construction. Include head to feet in all panels and do not crop the hem. If only product references are supplied, choose one fictional model once and keep that model consistent. If multiple model identities are supplied, ask which one should appear in the three depictions. No added brand names or captions.",
'P13':"Translate the reference portrait into a close layered paper-relief artwork. Create cheek and nose planes through torn, cut, folded and stacked paper, with real edge thickness, visible fibres and shallow cast shadows, not a flat texture filter. Use warm umber, indigo, cream and grey paper tones; preserve the reference's relative complexion values and distinguishing age cues in the material translation. Curve monsoon-cloud forms behind the head, never across the eyes. Keep the original gentle expression and recognizable mouth asymmetry, eye spacing and hairline. No unrelated collage faces, stereotyped facial simplification or age reduction. Soft gallery side light reveals the physical relief.",
'P17':"Stand the supplied perfume bottle upright and dry on a clear acrylic plinth. A single clean water arc rises behind it like a transient architectural arch. Preserve the actual bottle, cap, label, logo, geometry, materials and liquid level. Water never passes through the glass or obscures the front label, and never appears to emerge from the bottle. Neutral front label fill, crisp water edge lights and a charcoal-blue background. Contain the complete arch and bottle with breathing room; avoid reflections that imply a second bottle. This constructed campaign makes no waterproofness claim. Without a product reference, first establish one original fictional clear-glass bottle with a bronze cap and blank cream label, then preserve that fixture for the campaign."
}
existing={p['slug']:p for f in ['content/prompts.json','content/expansion/prompts.json','content/additions/friends-trip-prompts.json'] for p in json.loads(Path(f).read_text())}
out=[]
for r in rows:
 pid=r['id'];slug=r['detail_url'].split('/')[-1]
 if pid.startswith('E'):
  out.append({'id':pid,'slug':slug,'canonical_path':r['detail_url'],'action':'retain-copy-unchanged','prompt_text':existing[slug]['prompt_text']});continue
 blocks=[]
 if pid!='P17':
  blocks.append(art_reference if pid in ['P05','P13'] else photo_reference)
  blocks.append('NO REFERENCE PRESENT: Default to an appropriate fictional Indian/South Asian '+fallback[pid]+'. Use believable diversity of age, complexion, hair and natural build. The preview persona is an example, not a fixed default face. '+('For a fictional garment example, use a simple indigo saree with a narrow copper border and matching blouse; supplied product references always override that example.' if pid=='P12' else ''))
 if pid in ['P12','P17']:blocks.append(product_reference)
 blocks.extend(['CREATIVE DIRECTION:',bodies[pid], 'OUTPUT: '+r['ratio']+' portrait artwork. Keep faces and essential objects inside the frame. No watermark or unwanted text. Keep anatomy, depth and shadows coherent for the declared medium. Compare the result with the supplied references; if details drift, make a focused edit or composite the original source rather than accepting a different identity.'])
 out.append({'id':pid,'slug':slug,'canonical_path':r['detail_url'],'action':'update-existing-id' if r['proposal']['existing_prompt_slug'] else 'new-record','transformation_type':r['mechanism'],'prompt_text':'\n\n'.join(blocks),'image_brief':r['image_prompt'],'reference_requirements':r['proposal']['references'],'preview_persona':r['proposal']['preview_brief'],'why_ai':r['proposal']['why_ai'],'distinctiveness_score':r['score'],'draft_for_integration':True})
(root/'copyable-prompts.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
print('Prepared twelve copyable texts, including unchanged retained prompts; no live content altered.')
